{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff (owner of `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`). The 14 entries of `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/pid-liveness.args` belong to this bug.\n\n## Root cause (verified from the Windows JUnit of run 44681457334 and the code at origin/main 863abe7cd19)\nThere are 2 defects. One is in the product and one is in the tests.\n\n1. **Product: Windows has no pid liveness probe.** `rebar._store.lock_owner._pid_alive` returns True whenever `_signal_zero_probes_liveness()` is False, which is the Windows case (`os.kill(pid, 0)` there calls TerminateProcess). So a dead holder is never proven dead on Windows:\n   - `_describe_stamped_pid` reports `unverified-live` instead of `not-running` (`test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084`).\n   - Stamped and mkdir locks of dead owners are never reclaimed on that proof (`test_stamped_lock` x2, `test_lock_stale_reclaim`, `test_stale_lock_reclaim_write`).\n   - The test helpers that search downward for a non-running pid with `while _pid_alive(pid)` never terminate, so the xdist worker dies (`test_doctor_locks` x6, `test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d`: \"worker crashed\").\n   Windows can probe liveness without signalling. `OpenProcess(SYNCHRONIZE | PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION, pid)` fails with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER (87) when no process has that id. `WaitForSingleObject(handle, 0)` returns WAIT_OBJECT_0 once the process has exited, and WAIT_TIMEOUT (0x102) while it runs.\n2. **Tests: `Popen([sys.executable, ...]).pid` is not the interpreter's pid on the sweep.** The sweep's venv comes from `uv venv`, whose `Scripts\\python.exe` is a launcher that starts the real interpreter as a child process. The stamp records the child's `os.getpid()`, while the test asserts the launcher's `proc.pid`:\n   - `test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084`: expected `pid=7556`, stamp `pid=7536`.\n   - `test_mcp_idle_sync`: expected 9012, stamp 8428.\n   - `proc.kill()` kills only the launcher, so the lock-holding interpreter keeps running (`test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084`).\n   - Separately, 2 dead-pid helpers spawn `[\"true\"]`, which does not exist on Windows (`test_lock_stale_reclaim`, `test_stale_lock_reclaim_write`).\n\n## Approach\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py`:\n  - Add `_windows_pid_alive(pid, kernel32=None)`. It is ctypes-only and takes an injectable kernel32 for tests. It never signals.\n    - OpenProcess fails with 87: dead (False).\n    - OpenProcess fails with any other error (e.g. 5, access denied): alive (True).\n    - WaitForSingleObject(h, 0) == 0: exited (False).\n    - Any other wait result: alive (True).\n    - The handle is always closed with CloseHandle.\n  - `_pid_alive` keeps the POSIX signal-0 path. Where signal 0 is not a probe it uses `_windows_pid_alive` when `os.name == \"nt\"`, and otherwise returns True as today.\n  - Docstrings updated. No config key, env var or flag.\n- Tests:\n  - A shared helper in `tests/_python_child.py`, `spawn_python(code, *args) -> (proc, pid)`. The child prints `os.getpid()` as its first stdout line, and the helper returns that real interpreter pid.\n  - `test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084`, `test_mcp_idle_sync` and `test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084` assert that pid. They terminate the holder with `os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)`, then `proc.kill()`/`wait()`.\n  - `test_lock_stale_reclaim` and `test_stale_lock_reclaim_write` spawn `[sys.executable, \"-c\", \"\"]` instead of `[\"true\"]`.\n- `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py`: the conservative-seam test keeps asserting that no `os.kill` is sent. On a non-nt host the answer stays True.\n- New `tests/unit/store/test_windows_pid_probe.py`:\n  - A fake kernel32 covers the 4 OpenProcess/wait outcomes and checks that CloseHandle is called.\n  - On Windows only, a real spawned-and-reaped child reads dead, and our own pid reads alive.\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/pid-liveness.args`: remove each line whose test passes in the tmp-branch Windows run. If the file ends up empty, delete it and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml`; `tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` keeps the 2 in step.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py\n- tests/_python_child.py\n- tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_sync.py\n- tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py\n- tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py\n- tests/interfaces/store/test_stale_lock_reclaim_write.py\n- tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py\n- tests/unit/store/test_windows_pid_probe.py\n- .github/windows-sweep-deselect/pid-liveness.args\n- .github/workflows/test.yml (only if the args file is deleted)\n\n## Testing\n- Fake-kernel32 unit tests run on every host.\n- Windows proof: push the exact tree to `tmp/b4-smoking-bereft-boar` and dispatch `gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/b4-smoking-bereft-boar`. That runs `sweep (windows)` with the fixed lines removed from the args file. Record the run id and the per-test outcomes here, then delete the tmp branch.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `pid-liveness.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `pid-liveness.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795256364826774001,"uuid":"9ce629b5-1598-4599-a542-8c5dc4348f24"}